# zl1-installers-selftest.sh -- mutations, and the same harness against the PRE-FIX installer
# 2026-09-23
#
# Baseline: sh scripts/host/zl1-installers-selftest.sh   ->   pass=336 fail=0 skip=0 (rc=0)
#
# The fix under test (docs 114) is the pair of gates on the v63 debug keeper's retirement:
#   * the replacement gate   -- the applier kills only if /etc/systemd/system/zl1-netwatch.sh is
#     executable, carries `ensure_addrs()`, and zl1-netwatch.service is active; otherwise it exits 1
#     so the unit lands in `systemctl --failed` (a silent unarmed heat fix is worse, docs 99);
#   * the licence gate       -- `--now` without `--after-proof` exits 2 having touched nothing; with
#     it, the installer pushes device/zl1-address-owner-proof.sh, runs it under `timeout -k 5 120`,
#     and kills only on the exact line `== verdict: proof-obtained`.
#
# Every mutation is applied to a COPY of the whole scripts/ tree (cp -a), and the harness is run with
# the REPOSITORY as the working directory. That last part is load-bearing and was measured, not
# assumed: the "shipped applier" section walks `git log -- scripts/install-cpufreq-governor.sh`, so a
# copy standing outside the repository has no history to walk -- it SKIPs that section (335 checks, 1
# skip) and the checks that depend on it then fail. The first version of this runner ran from /tmp and
# reported a BASE with 4 failures, none of them about the code under test.
#
# Each mutation ASSERTS its own edit landed before the harness is run: a mutation that changes nothing
# and a check that tests nothing are the same object (docs 113 section 5).

===== BASE (no mutation) =====
